Register session A then B; invoke A tool/slash command with A context: sender_session is B. A pre_llm hook returns B-only mail and empties B mock inbox. identity.py global current_alias/session, C2cCli environment and handlers ignore invocation identity. Require session-bound immutable subprocess environments and exact invocation ownership checks across registration/hooks/tools/commands. Unknown target fails closed before any send/drain/env mutation. Include interleaved multi-session/profile regression tests.

## Evidence and scope
Isolated mocked probes against installed ~/.hermes/plugins/c2c; seven Python files match c2c data/hermes-plugin. Reproduced by parent via PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 ~/.hermes/cache/scratch/c2c-session-probe.py; results sibling c2c-session-probe-results.json. No live mail, services or configuration touched. Preserve/rehome regression fixture into repo tests before scratch expires. These are isolated reproductions, not observed production disclosure/loss. Coordinate with I016 and B371; separate from frozen b8 B369/B370 relay candidate. No compilation on xsm; use buildboxes for required build gates.


Execution lane and decision (2026-10-22): Decision: one serial runtime lane for B372→B373→B374→B375 because identity.py, c2c_cli.py, hooks, delivery.py and watcher ownership overlap. Use per-session/profile immutable subprocess bindings, fail closed on missing/ambiguous invocation ownership, then target-key delivery, selective ack/durable preservation and atomic delivery reservation. Keep native hooks/MCP B098 data semantics. Rehome the supplied probe, test on x-p35 only.